From a4e846da4b8f0140e97f0c902808b9d5d3ed1bc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan Hill Norris <ewan.hillnorris@rapieruk.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:40:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Remove out-of-scope event step markers from event stream
 notebook

The event stream notebook carried 751 event step marker comments. Only
the steps listed in Missing_Event_Stream_Inserts.xlsx are in scope for
data collection, so any marker outside that list with no SQL written
against it is noise.

This removes 389 empty markers that are neither listed in
Missing_Event_Stream_Inserts.xlsx nor have any code in place, plus the
39 notebook cells left empty as a result.

Kept in full:
- all 284 step ids listed in Missing_Event_Stream_Inserts.xlsx
- all 143 markers that already have SQL against them (inserts, count
  queries, staging table builds and exploratory selects)

362 markers remain. Every non-comment SQL line is byte for byte
unchanged, verified by diff.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MEWc5KY6FCfLMaPieR9TLE
---
